pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Asking Someone to Repeat", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use modals of request like \"<span class=\"italic\">Would ...</span> \" and \"<span class=\"italic\">Can ...</span>\" and  these phrases below to ask someone to repeat something:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Polite </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Casual </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm sorry, could you repeat that, please?<br />Would you say that again, please?<br/>Pardon me?<br />Can you repeat that, please?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Again, please?<br />Can you say that again?<br />What was that?<br />Come again?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Hobbies and Interests", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In warm seasons, like summer and spring, people have hobbies, and we can use the Simple Present tense to talk about them. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " For example: <br>I love gardening in the summer. <br> I go swimming on Sundays. <br> I enjoy surfing with my brother.<br>I go cycling regularly.<br>My friends would like to start bird-watching with me.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In cold seasons, like winter, people have hobbies, like:<br />skiing <br />ice-skating <br />snowboarding", "type": "text"}, {"content": " ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "wrong ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not correct", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That is the wrong answer. Try again.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le02ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you want to return something.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "right ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "correct ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That is the right answer! Good work!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le02ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to realize ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to understand something you didn't know before ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I just realized that comic books are expensive!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le02ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to return ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to take something back to a store ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have to return this book - it's the wrong one.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le02ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "receipt ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a piece of paper that lists the things you buy at a store ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You need the receipt to return an item at a store.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le02ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to exchange ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to return something at a store and get another thing to replace it ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can exchange the book for another one.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le02ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "return policy ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the rules for returning something to a store ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What is the return policy at the store?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le02ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to rip ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make a hole in clothing or paper ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Oh no, I ripped the book!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le02ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "amazing ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "excellent; fantastic ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The illustrations are amazing!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le02ob03aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn3le02ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a short dialogue (5-6 lines).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask the clerk about their return policy.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask them to repeat what they say.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice the dialogue with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a short dialogue in a store setting.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask for repetition.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask about a return policy.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}